    "title": "Maryland residents debate whether to send more trash to Virginia - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By RADIO IQ ,\n5 hours ago People concerned about air and water quality may assume that a plant burning garbage is bad for the environment, which is why residents of Maryland’s Montgomery County – with a population of 1.2 million – are talking about closing their incinerator – which has operated for 30 years -- and trucking trash to one of two Virginia landfill in Chesterfield or Amelia Counties. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
